@startuml
title Agent Teams Workflow v2 — authority and data boundaries
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFAF8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #553C35
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Wallet holder" as wallet #FFD4BA
package "Public interaction" #E2F1FA {
  component F1r3sky #CDE7F5
  component "Run inspector" as inspector #CDE7F5
}
package "Embers trust boundary" #FFF0DB {
  component "Schema + graph validator" as validator #FFD5AC
  component "Rholang compiler" as compiler #FFD5AC
  component "Reply redactor / limiter" as limiter #FFD5AC
}
package "Capability boundary" #E7F3E7 {
  database "RSpace" as rspace #CBE7CC
  component "Team unforgeable name" as teamcap #B9DCBE
  component "Opaque run UUID" as runcap #B9DCBE
}
package "Effect boundary" #EEE6F8 {
  component "Pinned agent code" as agent #DDD0F0
  component "Model and media services" as models #DDD0F0
}

wallet --> validator : signed definition / run
validator --> compiler : publishable typed IR only
compiler --> teamcap : deploy
teamcap --> rspace : read/write private workflow state
rspace --> agent : explicit capability invocation
agent --> models : explicit service channels
limiter --> F1r3sky : <latex>\le 280</latex> chars + URL
runcap --> inspector : bearer read authority
inspector --> rspace : metadata only

note right of rspace #FFF6C9
Never place prompts, outputs, credentials,
or artifact bytes in the public run ledger.
end note
note bottom of compiler #FAD8D8
Pure Rholang guards reject binding,
communication, URI, and effectful forms.
end note
@enduml
